  "summary_en": "Pyro Vortex Confinement Force applies a vortex confinement force to a velocity field. It strengthens existing vortices to offset detail lost to diffusion during the fluid solver's diffusion stages. It outputs the modified velocities v.",
  "inputs": [
    "v: Vector VDB containing the original velocities",
    "direction: Vector VDB for per-voxel control of the force direction",
    "threshold: Float or Vector VDB used as a threshold mask; a Vector VDB contributes its length",
    "control: Float or Vector VDB used as a control mask; a Vector VDB contributes its length",
    "angledir: Vector VDB for per-voxel control of the angle mask direction"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Activation: 1 turns the node on, 0 turns it off; the node has no effect unless set to 1",
    "Operation: Set (replace), Add, or Rotate (align with the incoming velocity direction)",
    "Type: First-order (fast and stable, more numerical diffusion) or second-order (better detail and energy preservation, slower and possibly unstable)",
    "Confinement Scale: strength of the confinement force",
    "Positive / Negative Diffusion Scale: positive smooths noise and spikes for stability; negative acts as anti-diffusion, concentrating energy toward vortex centres",
    "Kernel Size: size of the stencil used to compute curvature; larger gives smoother results",
    "Target Energy: smoothly clamps amplification above a set band energy to reduce instability",
    "Adaptive Confinement: limits confinement to areas where vortices are likely to form, reducing jitter",
    "Frequency Separation (Min/Max Swirl Size): restricts which swirl sizes are affected",
    "Threshold, Control, Angle and Axis masks: scale the effect by a range or direction, with optional ramps; Angle Mask uses Spread Angle (default 90 degrees), Axis Mask uses a world-space Axis Range"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Requires DOP-level permissions. Not available in Houdini Core; works in FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education.",
    "The second-order method can introduce instabilities; the diffusion scale parameters are the suggested mitigation.",
    "Kernel Size and Frequency Separation both remove high-frequency detail, so aggressive values may remove useful detail.",
    "The node has no effect unless Activation is 1."
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Ce nœud renforce les tourbillons existants d'un champ de vitesse pour compenser la perte de détail due à la diffusion du solveur."
